cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ABMfact, please cite it as below."
title: "ABMfact: is it a finding or an artefact?"
abstract: >-
  ABMfact audits the conclusions of agent-based models against implementation artefacts. It reruns a
  model under changes that a correct implementation must not care about, such as activation order,
  agent labels, random streams, grid placement, time step and population size, and reports which
  stated conclusions survive, with intervals and reproducible commands.
type: software
authors:
